          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "stereotipo is usually traced to French stéréotype, a printing word built from Greek stereós \"solid\" and týpos \"a blow, an impression\", the word behind Latin typus \"a figure, an image\" (Lewis & Short): a fixed plate that prints the same image again and again."
            }
          ]
